    "notes": "L6 edge case. e01 migrates a small DNS set; this widens record-type coverage (A/AAAA/CNAME proxied+unproxied, MX priorities, TXT SPF/DKIM/DMARC, CAA, SRV, HTTPS/SVCB) and the proxied-flag matrix so a type-specific migration regression is caught. assertProxiedFlagsMatch checks proxied flags on proxiable records; assertDnsRecordTypesPresent independently guards record-type BREADTH (every declared record must be present on dest) so a non-proxiable type that fails to seed or migrate — e.g. CAA/SRV/HTTPS, which require a structured `data` object, not a flat content string — surfaces as a failure instead of a silent pass. All names use the test.example.com placeholder (rewritten to SOURCE_DOMAIN at load). Only proxiable types (A/AAAA/CNAME) carry proxied=true.",
